* Generic (non-PDK) NMOS+PMOS corner models standing in for sky130's own
* tt/ss/ff process split -- identical to
* benchmarks/design-agent/reference/five-transistor-ota/models.lib (same
* "runs anywhere ngspice runs" precedent as examples/kb/rc-relaxation-
* oscillator/corners.lib). VTO/KP/LAMBDA move together within each corner
* section the way a real sky130 corner split would move both devices'
* drive strength and output resistance together. Replace with a real
* sky130 model library (models.pdk / models.lib pointing at $PDK_ROOT) once
* this task is re-run against real devices -- see README.md "Known
* limitation" note.
.model bench_nmos NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=0.55 KP=100u LAMBDA=0.04)
.model bench_pmos PMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=-0.55 KP=40u LAMBDA=0.05)

.lib tt
.model bench_nmos NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=0.50 KP=120u LAMBDA=0.05)
.model bench_pmos PMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=-0.50 KP=48u LAMBDA=0.06)
.endl tt

.lib ss
.model bench_nmos NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=0.60 KP=95u LAMBDA=0.04)
.model bench_pmos PMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=-0.60 KP=38u LAMBDA=0.05)
.endl ss

.lib ff
.model bench_nmos NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=0.40 KP=145u LAMBDA=0.06)
.model bench_pmos PMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=-0.40 KP=58u LAMBDA=0.07)
.endl ff
